[agent] ## Result
[agent] The diverging feature is **`f3`**.
[agent] **How I found it** — all work ran on Databricks (CLI mode):
[agent] 1. Uploaded both CSVs to a Unity Catalog volume `workspace.mlpab261212.data` and loaded them into tables `workspace.mlpab261212.training` (300 rows) and `workspace.mlpab261212.serving` (200 rows) via `read_files`.
[agent] 2. Joined on `entity_id` — all 200 serving entities matched a training row.
[agent] 3. Per-feature divergence count over the join: `f1, f2, f4, f5` matched exactly (0 diffs); **`f3` differed in all 200 rows**.
[agent] **Cause** — the difference is an exact, deterministic transform, not noise: `training_f3 = log1p(serving_f3)` (equivalently `serving_f3 = expm1(training_f3)`), verified with max error ~6e-7 across all rows. The training pipeline applies a `log1p` transform to f3, but the online serving path serves the raw untransformed value, skipping the `log1p` step — classic training/serving skew.
[agent] Written to `submission/answers.json`:
[agent] ```json
[agent] {"feature": "f3", "cause": "... training applies log1p to f3, serving serves the raw value ..."}
[agent] ```
